    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="37">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 37</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">{LXXXI} Se cirlesca mon se ðe oft betygen wære ðiefðe, ⁊ þonne æt siðestan synnigne gefó in ceape oððe elles æt openre scylde: slea him mon hond óf oððe fót.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">A man of the rank of ceorl, who has often been accused of theft, and finally, then, is openly caught either with the goods or in the unlawful act: let his hand or foot be struck off.</ab>
        <ab type="secondTranslation" xml:lang="en">If a commoner has often been accused of theft and is at last proved guilty, either in the ordeal or by being caught in the act of committing an offence, his hand or foot shall be struck off.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Se ciorlesca mon, þe oft betogen wære þiefðe, ⁊ þonne æt siðestan cyrre synnigne gefó in eeace oþþe æt openre scylde elles, slea him mon hond oððe fot.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
